Because, like, if I'm looking at my coffee cup, the fiber doesn't contain the quantum state of every single electron in the ceramic.

07:42.600 --> 07:46.500
If it did, the fiber would be infinite and totally useless.

07:46.740 --> 07:47.200
Exactly.

07:47.200 --> 07:52.000
And the paper brings up Gregory Bateson here, the famous anthropologist and systems theorist.

07:52.100 --> 07:55.240
To narrow this down, Bateson's contribution is vital here.

07:55.380 --> 08:00.820
He famously defined information in a cybernetic system as a difference which makes a difference.

08:00.900 --> 08:02.620
A difference which makes a difference.

08:02.720 --> 08:05.060
That is such a brilliant recursive phrase.

08:05.340 --> 08:08.300
It is brilliant because it establishes a filter for relevance.

08:08.300 --> 08:14.140
It highlights that a physical variation in a system only matters if it triggers a change in a subsequent state.

08:14.380 --> 08:14.460
Right.

08:14.540 --> 08:15.940
