15:18.760 --> 15:22.480
Curvature in our distinction bundle measures exactly this non-commutativity.

15:22.480 --> 15:24.280
It asks a geometric question.

15:25.000 --> 15:33.660
If we start at point A and we take two slightly different historical paths to get to point B, do we end up with the exact same menu of future options when we arrive?

15:33.980 --> 15:34.840
And if the answer is no.

15:35.040 --> 15:37.140
